course: dictionary
lesson: 4745
title: Horseman: one word, many riders
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A horseman is a man who rides a horse. A horsewoman is a woman who rides one. Horseman is made of two words joined together: horse and man.
explain: The word can mean a good rider: «a skilled horseman» rides very well. In history and stories it can mean a soldier or traveller on horseback, so the clues in the sentence show you which meaning fits.
explain: Read «a lone horseman» and think about the words around it. If the story is about a battle or a message, the horseman is probably a soldier or messenger. Always test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A horseman is a man who rides a horse; a woman who does this is a horsewoman.
fact: The plural of horseman is horsemen, and the plural of horsewoman is horsewomen.
fact: «Rich horsemen trained from boyhood» were knights, who wore heavy armour in battle.
fact: Zhang Qian was held prisoner by the Xiongnu, «horsemen of the northern steppe», for about ten years.
fact: The Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse are four riders in the Book of Revelation who stand for war, famine, disease and death.
exercise: «Their best fighters were knights, rich horsemen trained from boyhood.» In this sentence, what is a horseman? | A kind of carriage | *A rider trained to fight on horseback | A person who cleans stables | A type of horse
exercise: «The headless horseman is an old legend, made famous in a story by Washington Irving.» What is a legend? | A true report from a newspaper | A map showing roads | A kind of horse | *An old story, often not known to be true
exercise: What is the feminine form of horseman? | Horselady | Horsemaid | *Horsewoman | Horsegirl
test: «Pechenegs, horsemen of the steppe, killed Prince Sviatoslav in 972.» What does horsemen tell you about the Pechenegs? | *They fought on horseback | They sailed on ships | They were kings of a city | They were monks who prayed
test: In the Book of Revelation, what do the Four Horsemen stand for? | Sunshine and rain | *War, famine, disease and death | Sports and games | Wealth and music
exam: Which word is the feminine form of horseman? | horsecart | horsefriend | *horsewoman | horseboy
